USE RESTRICTIONS INHERITED FROM EMONET-FACE-HQ

Its dataset card states that the corpus, and models trained on it, must not be
used in sensitive, high-stakes domains. That covers, at least:

  * emotion recognition in workplaces or educational settings
  * real-time or retrospective surveillance in public spaces
  * law enforcement, border control, or asylum decisions
  * credit scoring, insurance, or hiring decisions
  * any application involving manipulation, deception, or unlawful
    discrimination

These restrictions are the corpus authors', not conditions of CC BY 4.0. We
reproduce them because this repository ships artifacts derived from that corpus,
and because the paper's own finding is that scores in this domain are easy to
mistake for measurements of perception.
